// waiver: the two-sentence oracle phrasing ("Each Vampire creature card you own
// that isn't on the battlefield has madness. The madness cost is equal to its
// mana cost.") is beyond the renderer. The `Each(SelectAll(..),
// GainAbility(Keyword(Madness(ManaCostOf(..)))))` static below renders as the
// bare anthem "All creatures have madness." — the renderer drops the complex
// SelectAll scope (Vampire ∧ owned-by-you ∧ off-battlefield) to "All", omits
// the `ManaCostOf` madness cost, and has no second cost sentence.
//
// The card static is BOTH the faithful printed-text model AND the sole
// functional source. The engine's derived-ability enumeration
// (`derive::derived_abilities_of`, read by the replacement gather and trigger
// scan) folds in the [CR#613] layer view's granted abilities, so the madness
// this static grants — scoped exactly right by the layer system: active only
// while the Gorger is on the battlefield ([CR#611.3b]), reaching only its
// controller's OWN off-battlefield Vampires via `Owner(Ref(You))` — opens the
// [CR#616.1] discard window on those cards. No companion global `ConferralRule`
// is used: a `ConferralRule` has no source object, so it could express neither
// the "you own" nor the "while a Gorger is on the battlefield" gate and would
// leak madness to every off-battlefield Vampire in the game.
Normal(
  name: "Falkenrath Gorger",
  mana_cost: [
    Red,
  ],
  types: [
    Creature,
  ],
  subtypes: [
    Vampire,
    Berserker,
  ],
  abilities: [
    // "Vampire creature CARD you own that isn't on the battlefield" — a creature
    // card in any non-battlefield zone, NOT a creature permanent, so the scope
    // uses the zone-agnostic `Type(Creature)` atom rather than the `Creature`
    // filter macro (which expands to `Permanent ∧ Type Creature`, i.e. requires
    // the battlefield and would contradict the `Not(InZone(Battlefield))` gate).
    Static(Each(
      SelectAll(And([Type(Creature), Subtype(Vampire), Owner(Ref(You)), Not(InZone(Battlefield))])),
      Modify(It, GainAbility(Keyword(Madness([ManaCostOf(EventObject)])))),
    )),
  ],
  power: 2,
  toughness: 1,
)
